\title{taxifydb: Build Backbones and Enrichments for the taxify Package}
\description{
Build pipeline for the \href{https://github.com/gcol33/taxify}{taxify} package.
Downloads raw source data from official providers (WFO, COL, GBIF, ITIS,
NCBI Taxonomy, Open Tree of Life, WoRMS, Euro+Med PlantBase, Index Fungorum,
AlgaeBase) and a wide set of trait and conservation datasets, normalizes
to a unified Darwin Core-like schema, and writes pre-compiled \code{.vtr}
files that the taxify runtime consumes.
}
\details{
Separates build-time concerns (network access, parsing, schema
normalization) from runtime concerns so that taxify itself stays lean.
}
\section{Backbone build pipeline}{

Each backend has a \verb{build_<name>()} function that:
\enumerate{
\item Downloads the raw source archive.
\item Parses it into a data.frame.
\item Calls \code{\link[=normalize_backbone]{normalize_backbone()}} to map to the unified schema.
\item Calls \code{\link[=precompute_backbone]{precompute_backbone()}} to add matching keys and embed
synonym resolution.
\item Calls \code{\link[=build_vtr]{build_vtr()}} to write the final \code{.vtr} with indexes and
metadata sidecar.
}
}

\section{Enrichment build pipeline}{

Each enrichment is registered with a download URL, parse function, and
optional group column. The build pipeline runs:
\enumerate{
\item Download + parse to a data.frame with \code{canonical_name} + trait
columns.
\item Pass through \code{\link[=resolve_enrichment_names]{resolve_enrichment_names()}} to expand names across
all 7 backbones.
\item Call \code{\link[=build_enrichment_vtr]{build_enrichment_vtr()}} to write the indexed \code{.vtr} plus
\code{meta.json} sidecar.
}
}

